name: ios-architecture
description: Layer boundaries and architectural rules for PickOne
---

# Layering

The application must preserve this dependency direction:

`Presentation -> Domain -> Data`

# Presentation Rules

- Views, view models, and presentation models live here.
- Presentation depends on use cases only.
- Presentation must not import or depend directly on repository implementations, DTOs, persistence, or API clients.

# Domain Rules

- Domain contains entities, snapshots, repository protocols, and use cases.
- Domain owns business rules.
- Domain must not know about SwiftUI, DTOs, UserDefaults, or networking details.

# Data Rules

- Data implements repository protocols and adapts external/storage models into domain models.
- DTOs must not leak outside Data.
- Mapping belongs in Data or Presentation, depending on the boundary being crossed.

# Snapshot Rules

- Use cases return immutable domain snapshots where screen state requires them.
- Snapshots are not presentation models.
- View models transform snapshots into UI state.

# View State Rules

- Views should render explicit state.
- Avoid hidden behavior in views when that behavior belongs in a view model or use case.
